# Spout Project Context

Go monorepo. Two binaries sharing `internal/` packages:
- `cmd/spout/` - CLI (pipe mode, run mode, session management)
- `cmd/server/` - standalone server (same code as `spout server`)

Server is the same binary everywhere (local, self-hosted, spout.sh).
Tiers are encryption modes, not different products.

## Architecture

```
CLI ──WebSocket──→ Server ──WebSocket──→ Browser (xterm.js)
```

- CLI reads raw bytes, batches (16ms / 64KB), sends binary WebSocket
- Server stores in memory + file, broadcasts to viewer WebSocket channels
- Browser renders with xterm.js (CDN, no parsing needed)
- Two WS libraries: coder/websocket (CLI, net/http) + fasthttp/websocket (server, Fiber)

## Key packages

- `internal/server/` - Fiber app, routes, WebSocket handlers
- `internal/store/` - Session struct, in-memory + file persistence, broadcast
- `internal/names/` - word-xxxx name generation

## Conventions

- Wrap errors: `fmt.Errorf("doing X: %w", err)`
- Table-driven tests, stdlib `testing`
- Copy fasthttp params before WebSocket upgrade (buffer reuse)
- No CGo, no JS build step
- `web/static/` → sync to `internal/server/static/` after edits

